From b272882c5c2d71cbb2120ed0df4038a54a4b05f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:55:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(sdk): lifecycle hygiene in the SDK (Decryption
 Authority Lifecycle, Level 2)

- A typed refusal. When the ACL precheck refuses and an account the
  request rests on is retired (ACL.isAccountRetired), the precheck throws
  AclAccountRetiredError (code ACCOUNT_RETIRED, the retired accounts). It
  extends AclUserDecryptionError, so existing handlers still catch it.
  An allowed request makes no extra call. On an ACL without the lifecycle
  Core the generic error stays.
- getAuthorityStatus(client, { address }) and getAuthorityStatusOnChains:
  whether the ACL supports the lifecycle, whether the account is retired,
  and its E1 successor or pending designation.
- Transport-key hygiene. disposeTransportKeyPair zero-fills a key pair's
  private key, after which decrypting or serializing with it throws.
  createTransportKeyRing hands out one key pair per request, zero-fills it
  on release, and purges an account's key pairs and permits.
  purgeIfRetired purges them once the account is retired.

Unit tests with a mocked provider: 19 new tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
